1
00:00:20,911 --> 00:00:24,501
OCTOBER 1013 AD
LONDON, ENGLAND

2
00:00:29,501 --> 00:00:31,591
THE BATTLE OF LONDON BRIDGE

3
00:00:40,641 --> 00:00:43,061
That's not really a bridge.

4
00:00:43,141 --> 00:00:44,981
It's more like a fortress.

5
00:00:45,061 --> 00:00:47,151
I'm impressed, London.

6
00:00:47,231 --> 00:00:49,901
The city has survived many attacks
over the years.

7
00:00:49,981 --> 00:00:51,821
It has a lot of history.

8
00:00:51,901 --> 00:00:55,911
This isn't the time to be complacent, Askeladd.

9
00:00:55,991 --> 00:00:57,911
This city's going to be trouble.

10
00:00:57,991 --> 00:01:00,831
You said it'd be an easy win.
That's why I'm here.

11
00:01:00,911 --> 00:01:03,001
Sorry, sorry.

12
00:01:03,081 --> 00:01:07,251
I never imagined
that Thorkell would side with the enemy.

13
00:01:11,301 --> 00:01:13,711
You mean, Thorkell the Tall?

14
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:16,221
He's in bed with the enemy for the money.

15
00:01:16,301 --> 00:01:17,381
What a traitor.

16
00:01:19,261 --> 00:01:22,011
We're in this for the money too.

17
00:01:22,101 --> 00:01:26,231
We sided with the Army of Denmark,
because we thought King Sweyn has a chance to win.

18
00:01:30,611 --> 00:01:32,821
The other clans are all the same.

19
00:01:32,901 --> 00:01:36,151
They're desperate
to prove themselves on the battlefield

20
00:01:36,241 --> 00:01:39,321
and increase their share of the spoils.

21
00:01:39,411 --> 00:01:43,331
Well, with so many men here,
no one's getting very much.

22
00:01:45,121 --> 00:01:47,671
I don't fight for money.

23
00:01:47,751 --> 00:01:49,331
I like to kill.

24
00:01:51,251 --> 00:01:53,341
I can truly rely on a man like you, Bjorn.

25
00:01:53,421 --> 00:01:58,841
In any case, those bigwigs all want London.

26
00:01:59,511 --> 00:02:01,721
If we can capture the Thames River,

27
00:02:01,801 --> 00:02:04,721
we can set up a supply line
to the inland areas in Wessex.

28
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:09,231
The top leaders all have their eyes
on this battleground.

29
00:02:09,311 --> 00:02:13,021
Yeah. This is the place to be if you want to stand out.

30
00:02:14,071 --> 00:02:15,611
What do you mean?

31
00:02:15,691 --> 00:02:18,031
Do you have a plan in mind?

32
00:02:18,111 --> 00:02:19,491
Well,

33
00:02:19,571 --> 00:02:21,991
it's not really a plan.

34
00:02:22,531 --> 00:02:23,531
Thorfinn.

35
00:02:25,081 --> 00:02:27,501
We have some work for you.

36
00:02:27,581 --> 00:02:29,371
Go bring me Thorkell's head.

37
00:02:35,131 --> 00:02:37,381
Promise me you'll give me my reward.

38
00:02:37,461 --> 00:02:39,551
Okay. Okay.

39
00:02:39,631 --> 00:02:42,511
The same as always, right?
You're so stubborn.

40
00:02:43,051 --> 00:02:45,351
Getting so worked up about a fight you can't win.

41
00:02:45,431 --> 00:02:48,101
Maybe you get it from your father.

42
00:02:52,351 --> 00:02:54,521
Don't forget, Askeladd.

43
00:02:54,611 --> 00:02:56,231
My only wish as a warrior

44
00:02:56,321 --> 00:02:59,701
is to beat you in a duel.

45
00:02:59,781 --> 00:03:03,161
Our next duel will be your last.

46
00:03:03,241 --> 00:03:05,241
I'm going to carve out your heart,

47
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:07,831
and offer it to my father's spirit.

48
00:03:12,211 --> 00:03:13,961
Then get to work.

49
00:03:14,041 --> 00:03:17,591
Only those who fight
on the battlefield get what they desire.

50
00:03:17,671 --> 00:03:20,221
That's the way of the warrior.

51
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:27,101
My head's not cheap, you know.

52
00:03:27,181 --> 00:03:30,851
I'll duel you as often as you like.

53
00:03:32,231 --> 00:03:35,231
Go bring me Thorkell's head.

54
00:05:10,831 --> 00:05:12,491
Hey.

55
00:05:12,581 --> 00:05:14,501
Askeladd.

56
00:05:15,081 --> 00:05:16,081
What?

57
00:05:16,171 --> 00:05:18,881
One ship is heading towards the bridge.

58
00:05:19,541 --> 00:05:23,131
It's the Jomsvikings! The Sea Deer!

59
00:05:23,711 --> 00:05:26,181
They're messengers from the regular army.

60
00:05:26,261 --> 00:05:27,511
Are they Floki's men?

61
00:05:28,681 --> 00:05:32,011
I bet he's going to try to win Thorkell over to his side

62
00:05:32,101 --> 00:05:35,391
by saying he'll pay double whatever England pays.

63
00:05:35,481 --> 00:05:37,351
Thorkell will follow the money.

64
00:05:37,441 --> 00:05:38,771
I bet he'll take their offer.

65
00:05:40,691 --> 00:05:43,401
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

66
00:05:45,031 --> 00:05:46,201
They're here.

67
00:05:46,281 --> 00:05:47,401
It's just one ship.

68
00:05:52,491 --> 00:05:54,411
This way. Hurry.

69
00:05:56,001 --> 00:05:58,171
Die. Take that.

70
00:05:58,251 --> 00:05:59,881
Take that.

71
00:05:59,961 --> 00:06:00,791
Fire. Fire.

72
00:06:01,381 --> 00:06:03,841
Don't shoot. We're messengers.

73
00:06:03,921 --> 00:06:06,171
We want to talk to Thorkell.

74
00:06:08,471 --> 00:06:09,931
-You damn bastards.
-Die.

75
00:06:10,551 --> 00:06:12,601
We didn't come here to fight.

76
00:06:12,681 --> 00:06:15,061
Where is Thorkell?

77
00:06:15,141 --> 00:06:18,231
Shut up. Die.

78
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:20,061
Hey.

79
00:06:20,151 --> 00:06:21,771
Stop.

80
00:06:21,861 --> 00:06:22,821
Yes, sir.

81
00:06:22,901 --> 00:06:25,691
Everyone. Cease fire.

82
00:06:28,901 --> 00:06:33,331
Hey, Floki. It's been a while.

83
00:06:33,411 --> 00:06:36,081
You look like you've been doing well.

84
00:06:36,161 --> 00:06:38,461
Enough with the pleasantries.

85
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:43,591
His Highness, King Sweyn, sends a message,
which I am here to deliver.

86
00:06:43,671 --> 00:06:45,841
In the words of His Highness:

87
00:06:46,881 --> 00:06:50,511
"The King of England has escaped
to the land of the Franks.

88
00:06:50,591 --> 00:06:53,101
Resistance is futile.

89
00:06:53,891 --> 00:06:55,641
Surrender.

90
00:06:55,721 --> 00:06:57,931
If you surrender, then in the name of Thor,

91
00:06:58,021 --> 00:07:00,641
I shall spare the lives of you and your men,

92
00:07:00,731 --> 00:07:03,111
as well as leave you your fortunes."

93
00:07:04,151 --> 00:07:07,151
Go back to the army, Thorkell.

94
00:07:07,231 --> 00:07:09,701
Those are the wishes of His Highness.

95
00:07:10,361 --> 00:07:12,781
Is King Sweyn here?

96
00:07:12,871 --> 00:07:14,241
He's tough.

97
00:07:14,321 --> 00:07:16,201
For such an old man.

98
00:07:16,291 --> 00:07:17,791
Thorkell.

99
00:07:17,871 --> 00:07:22,331
Why are you drawing your bow against a friend?

100
00:07:22,421 --> 00:07:27,461
For so long, we've fought as warriors, side by side.

101
00:07:28,511 --> 00:07:32,011
You must not misread the flow of the world.

102
00:07:32,091 --> 00:07:35,891
Your brother Sigvaldi is also worried.

103
00:07:37,351 --> 00:07:39,731
Flow of the world?

104
00:07:39,811 --> 00:07:41,391
I see.

105
00:07:41,481 --> 00:07:46,571
I was fighting against the English myself until last year.
That's why I know.

106
00:07:46,651 --> 00:07:49,151
They're really weak.

107
00:07:49,231 --> 00:07:52,361
-They're a bunch of sheltered city boys.
-What?

108
00:07:52,451 --> 00:07:53,911
-Is that Norse?
-They lack spirit.

109
00:07:53,991 --> 00:07:54,911
Maybe.

110
00:07:55,531 --> 00:07:59,081
Prince Edmund was the only general

111
00:07:59,161 --> 00:08:01,911
who could handle the army of Denmark.

112
00:08:02,001 --> 00:08:04,291
This country is finished.

113
00:08:04,371 --> 00:08:05,791
Oh, in that case...

114
00:08:05,881 --> 00:08:08,551
In other words,

115
00:08:09,251 --> 00:08:12,221
it'd be more fun

116
00:08:12,301 --> 00:08:14,931
to fight against you.

117
00:08:15,011 --> 00:08:16,431
What?

118
00:08:16,511 --> 00:08:18,511
That's enough talk.

119
00:08:18,601 --> 00:08:21,271
Let's get to the next part. The next part.

120
00:08:21,351 --> 00:08:23,561
Wait. Thorkell.

121
00:08:23,641 --> 00:08:28,111
I promise you double what England's giving you.

122
00:08:35,031 --> 00:08:38,451
Here I go, Floki.

123
00:08:38,531 --> 00:08:41,661
Veer left. Full speed.

124
00:08:42,251 --> 00:08:43,751
Time for the deadly...

125
00:08:43,831 --> 00:08:45,671
Keel-Buster!!

126
00:08:50,751 --> 00:08:53,421
Oh, I missed.

127
00:08:53,511 --> 00:08:54,551
Full speed.

128
00:08:54,631 --> 00:08:55,681
Withdraw.

129
00:08:58,261 --> 00:08:59,761
Men. Kill them.

130
00:08:59,851 --> 00:09:00,681
Yes, sir.

131
00:09:01,771 --> 00:09:04,021
Retreat. Retreat.

132
00:09:07,901 --> 00:09:10,191
Hey, Floki.

133
00:09:11,071 --> 00:09:13,651
Go ask King Sweyn

134
00:09:13,741 --> 00:09:18,161
whether he's bored
of always fighting battles he's going to win.

135
00:09:26,541 --> 00:09:29,381
There's no chance that we'll be able to convince him.

136
00:09:30,381 --> 00:09:31,841
I see.

137
00:09:31,921 --> 00:09:33,381
It was a waste of time.

138
00:09:33,461 --> 00:09:36,131
So, what shall we do?

139
00:09:41,971 --> 00:09:43,811
Attack them now, without delay.

140
00:10:02,371 --> 00:10:04,041
Hey. Damn.

141
00:10:16,471 --> 00:10:17,591
All right.

142
00:10:20,141 --> 00:10:22,721
Damn. They're attacking the pier.

143
00:10:24,221 --> 00:10:25,271
You bastard.

144
00:10:26,311 --> 00:10:27,601
Hurry.

145
00:10:27,681 --> 00:10:28,521
Damn.

146
00:10:28,601 --> 00:10:31,771
-Damn. I missed.
-Get more rocks.

147
00:10:31,861 --> 00:10:33,901
Out of my way.

148
00:10:33,981 --> 00:10:35,531
Wow.

149
00:10:35,611 --> 00:10:37,281
Here we go.

150
00:10:43,741 --> 00:10:46,451
How'd you like that?
That was my special...

151
00:10:46,541 --> 00:10:48,041
er... Log-Dropper!!

152
00:10:48,121 --> 00:10:49,371
The name says it all.

153
00:10:49,461 --> 00:10:50,501
That was amazing.

154
00:10:50,581 --> 00:10:51,751
Next.

155
00:10:51,831 --> 00:10:52,881
Hurry up.

156
00:10:52,961 --> 00:10:53,841
Yes, sir.

157
00:10:59,511 --> 00:11:02,011
What's wrong with Sweyn's army?

158
00:11:02,091 --> 00:11:04,301
Why don't you come up with something?

159
00:11:04,391 --> 00:11:07,471
I know you can do better if you try.

160
00:11:07,561 --> 00:11:12,731
At this rate, you won't capture London Bridge.
Not even in a hundred years...

161
00:11:24,201 --> 00:11:27,491
This is it. This guy looks fun.

162
00:11:27,581 --> 00:11:29,911
Thorfinn. Can you hear me?

163
00:11:30,001 --> 00:11:33,041
The huge man in front with the log.

164
00:11:33,131 --> 00:11:34,381
That's Thorkell.

165
00:11:35,461 --> 00:11:37,591
This is no good. Stop the ship.

166
00:11:37,671 --> 00:11:39,511
He'll hit us if we get any closer.

167
00:11:39,591 --> 00:11:41,221
Steer left.

168
00:11:41,301 --> 00:11:42,631
Just a little further.

169
00:11:45,221 --> 00:11:47,221
All right. That's enough.

170
00:11:47,311 --> 00:11:48,721
Jump.

171
00:11:49,431 --> 00:11:51,601
Don't touch him.

172
00:11:51,691 --> 00:11:54,101
This jolly little fool...

173
00:11:55,111 --> 00:11:57,901
is all mine.

174
00:11:58,821 --> 00:11:59,941
Yeah.

175
00:12:02,241 --> 00:12:03,361
Bastard.

176
00:12:06,581 --> 00:12:07,621
Come on.

177
00:12:17,541 --> 00:12:18,591
You're good...

178
00:12:19,631 --> 00:12:20,961
For a kid.

179
00:12:29,011 --> 00:12:31,311
Don't touch him.

180
00:12:32,021 --> 00:12:35,601
I'll answer the challenge of this suicide attacker.

181
00:12:38,021 --> 00:12:39,441
It's one-on-one.

182
00:12:43,991 --> 00:12:47,571
All right. Bring it on, kid.

183
00:12:48,331 --> 00:12:50,081
One-on-one, and unarmed?

184
00:12:50,661 --> 00:12:52,041
Don't underestimate me.

185
00:13:03,631 --> 00:13:06,261
Oh, he was aiming for my wrist.

186
00:13:06,341 --> 00:13:08,391
Good job, kid.

187
00:13:12,221 --> 00:13:14,311
I can see why he's so confident.

188
00:13:14,391 --> 00:13:16,651
With a body and fists as big as his,

189
00:13:16,731 --> 00:13:18,651
I'd be dead with one hit.

190
00:13:19,271 --> 00:13:20,981
I like you.

191
00:13:21,071 --> 00:13:23,531
I'm going to have some fun.

192
00:13:24,071 --> 00:13:24,901
What?

193
00:13:27,491 --> 00:13:28,871
Take that.

194
00:13:31,201 --> 00:13:32,291
Oops.

195
00:13:32,951 --> 00:13:33,791
Damn.

196
00:13:35,911 --> 00:13:37,671
That was close.

197
00:13:40,131 --> 00:13:41,041
I can't reach him.

198
00:13:42,341 --> 00:13:45,011
All his weak points are up high.

199
00:13:45,091 --> 00:13:46,721
Below his armpit.

200
00:13:46,801 --> 00:13:47,801
His neck.

201
00:13:47,881 --> 00:13:48,931
All right.

202
00:13:54,851 --> 00:13:55,981
He's low.

203
00:13:56,771 --> 00:13:58,231
So...

204
00:13:58,311 --> 00:13:59,481
I'll kick him.

205
00:13:59,561 --> 00:14:00,771
Run in there.

206
00:14:17,121 --> 00:14:18,961
That hurts.

207
00:14:19,041 --> 00:14:21,541
But I got you.

208
00:14:27,221 --> 00:14:28,551
You did it.

209
00:14:28,631 --> 00:14:29,881
Great, captain.

210
00:14:29,971 --> 00:14:30,801
Kill him.

211
00:14:30,891 --> 00:14:32,851
It's not over yet.

212
00:14:32,931 --> 00:14:35,181
Here we go.

213
00:14:37,521 --> 00:14:39,191
Oh, dear.

214
00:14:39,271 --> 00:14:40,731
This won't work.

215
00:14:40,811 --> 00:14:42,941
Thorfinn's getting beaten to a pulp.

216
00:14:43,611 --> 00:14:45,281
I guess it wasn't going to work.

217
00:14:45,361 --> 00:14:46,441
Yeah.

218
00:14:48,531 --> 00:14:49,701
Askeladd.

219
00:14:49,781 --> 00:14:51,111
That's the signal.

220
00:14:51,201 --> 00:14:53,371
Yeah. Then it's time to retreat.

221
00:14:54,661 --> 00:14:56,451
Retreat.

222
00:14:56,541 --> 00:14:58,331
Withdraw all units.

223
00:15:00,961 --> 00:15:02,921
What? No.

224
00:15:03,001 --> 00:15:06,501
The battle ended while I was playing with the kid.

225
00:15:06,591 --> 00:15:07,671
Hey, kid.

226
00:15:07,761 --> 00:15:09,591
It looks like they abandoned you.

227
00:15:09,671 --> 00:15:11,091
Poor kid.

228
00:15:11,181 --> 00:15:13,601
Even though you tried hard.

229
00:15:14,931 --> 00:15:16,601
What? Is he dead?

230
00:15:16,681 --> 00:15:17,771
Hey.

231
00:15:17,851 --> 00:15:19,231
Hey. Hey. Hey.

232
00:15:41,331 --> 00:15:44,001
You still haven't lost the will to fight?

233
00:15:44,081 --> 00:15:46,711
You're good, even though you're small.

234
00:15:51,631 --> 00:15:53,181
Warrior.

235
00:15:53,261 --> 00:15:55,051
Tell me your name.

236
00:16:01,351 --> 00:16:02,351
Thorfinn.

237
00:16:04,061 --> 00:16:05,521
Son of Thors.

238
00:16:05,611 --> 00:16:06,731
I'm Thorfinn.

239
00:16:07,821 --> 00:16:09,191
Thors?

240
00:16:09,281 --> 00:16:11,491
Hey. Thors? Do you mean...?

241
00:16:15,201 --> 00:16:17,121
Oh, there he goes.

242
00:16:19,701 --> 00:16:21,331
Captain, your orders?

243
00:16:21,411 --> 00:16:22,541
Shall we shoot him?

244
00:16:23,961 --> 00:16:25,541
Don't shoot.

245
00:16:25,631 --> 00:16:27,131
We'll let him go today.

246
00:16:28,881 --> 00:16:30,131
Hey.

247
00:16:30,211 --> 00:16:32,921
Warrior Thorfinn.

248
00:16:33,011 --> 00:16:35,051
That was fun.

249
00:16:35,141 --> 00:16:36,851
Let's do this again.

250
00:16:37,551 --> 00:16:40,561
Let's finish things off next time.

251
00:16:40,641 --> 00:16:43,101
Promise me.

252
00:16:53,781 --> 00:16:55,741
That hurts.

253
00:16:55,821 --> 00:16:56,781
Kill me, please.

254
00:16:56,871 --> 00:16:59,201
Does anyone want to be killed?

255
00:16:59,281 --> 00:17:01,241
I can kill you.

256
00:17:04,911 --> 00:17:06,501
He's not going to make it.

257
00:17:07,171 --> 00:17:09,001
He's been stabbed in the gut.

258
00:17:09,091 --> 00:17:10,301
We can't save him.

259
00:17:10,381 --> 00:17:13,421
Hey. Bring some onion soup over here.

260
00:17:13,511 --> 00:17:14,591
Torgrim.

261
00:17:14,671 --> 00:17:15,761
Take care of this.

262
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:23,851
I see.

263
00:17:23,931 --> 00:17:25,771
So, we can't capture London.

264
00:17:26,521 --> 00:17:27,441
No.

265
00:17:27,521 --> 00:17:29,771
It's not that we can't capture London.

266
00:17:29,861 --> 00:17:32,401
It will just take some time.

267
00:17:33,111 --> 00:17:36,031
Time? How much time, Floki?

268
00:17:36,111 --> 00:17:39,531
Yes. It depends on the size of their stockpile.

269
00:17:40,581 --> 00:17:41,871
One year.

270
00:17:41,951 --> 00:17:45,041
No. A half-year, if things go well.

271
00:17:45,121 --> 00:17:47,121
It's already autumn.

272
00:17:47,211 --> 00:17:50,541
We cannot spend so much time on just one city.

273
00:17:52,631 --> 00:17:55,511
The overall situation is most important.

274
00:17:55,591 --> 00:17:57,131
In everything we do,

275
00:17:57,221 --> 00:18:01,431
we must prioritize gaining control over all of England.

276
00:18:01,511 --> 00:18:02,351
Yes, sir.

277
00:18:03,391 --> 00:18:05,891
We shall move our main forces to the west.

278
00:18:05,981 --> 00:18:07,641
Leave 4000 soldiers

279
00:18:07,731 --> 00:18:10,901
to continue the siege on London.

280
00:18:10,981 --> 00:18:12,691
As you wish.

281
00:18:16,281 --> 00:18:20,451
The 4000 soldiers will be under the command of...

282
00:18:23,991 --> 00:18:26,501
Canute.

283
00:18:27,331 --> 00:18:30,121
This is a good chance to boost his standing.

284
00:18:30,211 --> 00:18:31,211
What?

285
00:18:32,461 --> 00:18:34,501
That's not what we agreed upon.

286
00:18:34,591 --> 00:18:38,261
The reason His Highness came
to serve as a good example for the people.

287
00:18:38,341 --> 00:18:39,631
That's what you said.

288
00:18:39,721 --> 00:18:42,391
Ragnar. Please, refrain.

289
00:18:42,471 --> 00:18:44,141
This is His Highness's will.

290
00:18:44,221 --> 00:18:47,891
Against Thorkell,
even the entire army stands no chance.

291
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:50,351
To defeat him with only one-fifth of the forces...

292
00:18:50,441 --> 00:18:51,271
It's impossible.

293
00:18:51,981 --> 00:18:55,021
Having so few men is the only way to help him.

294
00:18:55,111 --> 00:18:56,151
But...

295
00:18:56,231 --> 00:19:00,071
His Highness is unfamiliar with battle,
and is experiencing emotional distress.

296
00:19:00,151 --> 00:19:03,831
This is your responsibility, Ragnar.

297
00:19:05,411 --> 00:19:08,001
Maybe it's because of the teachings of Christ.

298
00:19:08,081 --> 00:19:12,631
He grew up to be faint of heart,
even though he's a man.

299
00:19:12,711 --> 00:19:15,341
It's because you spoiled him.

300
00:19:17,711 --> 00:19:19,511
I apologize.

301
00:19:20,551 --> 00:19:24,301
To Canute,
I shall leave the soldiers laying siege to London.

302
00:19:24,391 --> 00:19:28,221
You shall accompany him,
and provide support, as his assistant.

303
00:19:40,611 --> 00:19:41,611
Your Highness...

304
00:20:23,241 --> 00:20:25,451
My shoulder is dislocated.

305
00:20:25,531 --> 00:20:28,161
And my right ankle is sprained.

306
00:20:28,241 --> 00:20:30,451
And I have a few broken ribs.

307
00:20:32,541 --> 00:20:33,581
Damn it.

308
00:20:33,671 --> 00:20:35,381
That madman.

309
00:20:38,001 --> 00:20:39,381
Hey. Can you see them?

310
00:20:42,761 --> 00:20:45,511
Most of them have retreated.

311
00:20:45,591 --> 00:20:46,431
What?

312
00:20:46,511 --> 00:20:48,891
Does that mean...?

313
00:20:48,971 --> 00:20:50,011
Did we...

314
00:20:50,101 --> 00:20:51,181
win?

315
00:20:52,391 --> 00:20:53,601
We won?

316
00:20:53,691 --> 00:20:57,731
-They ran away with their tails between their legs?
-Then we have won.

317
00:20:58,771 --> 00:21:00,531
What?

318
00:21:00,611 --> 00:21:02,531
What's going on?

319
00:21:02,611 --> 00:21:04,651
We did it. We won.

320
00:21:04,741 --> 00:21:05,571
What?

321
00:21:05,661 --> 00:21:07,371
We won.

322
00:21:07,451 --> 00:21:09,081
Hey, hey.

323
00:21:09,161 --> 00:21:10,541
Hey.

324
00:21:10,621 --> 00:21:12,831
Let's fight some more.

325
00:21:12,911 --> 00:21:15,081
Hey. Hold on.

326
00:21:15,161 --> 00:21:16,211
Hey.

327
00:21:19,211 --> 00:21:21,591
You idiots.

328
00:21:22,261 --> 00:21:25,131
Are you giving up on London?

329
00:21:25,221 --> 00:21:28,091
Come back, you cowards.

330
00:21:28,181 --> 00:21:31,011
Fight me.

331
00:21:36,061 --> 00:21:39,151
Oh, what a pain.

332
00:21:39,231 --> 00:21:41,111
Thorkell, you bastard.

333
00:21:44,781 --> 00:21:47,491
Hey. What happened? You're alive?

334
00:21:47,571 --> 00:21:50,491
You look terrible.

335
00:21:51,581 --> 00:21:55,001
You had a bad opponent, Thorfinn.

336
00:21:58,331 --> 00:22:02,381
By the way, I'm going to march on Wessex.
What about you?

337
00:22:02,461 --> 00:22:05,381
If it hurts to walk, I'll just leave you here.

338
00:22:27,401 --> 00:22:29,571
We're going to get rich in Wessex.

339
00:22:29,661 --> 00:22:31,661
I can't wait.

340
00:22:31,741 --> 00:22:34,951
-You only got one arm.
-I can handle anyone.

341
00:22:35,041 --> 00:22:36,621
I'll kill them all.

342
00:22:51,591 --> 00:22:54,101
That was fun.

343
00:22:54,181 --> 00:22:56,181
Let's do this again.

344
00:23:00,981 --> 00:23:02,811
That madman.

345
00:23:05,531 --> 00:23:09,861
What's so enjoyable about battle?
